# E-1166: Given a random walk $s_0,s_1,\ldots$ in $\mathbb{Z}^2$, starting at the origin, let $f_k(x)$ count the number of $0\leq l\leq k$ such that $s_l=x$. Let\[F(k)=\{ x: f_k(x) = \max_y f_k(y)\}\]be the set of 'favourite values'. Is it true that\[\left\lvert \bigcup_{k\leq n}F(k)\right\rvert \leq (\log n)^{O(1)}\]almost surely, for all but finitely many $n$?
